cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "telemdrift: streaming change detection on a univariate telemetry channel"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark harness, not a streaming framework. Five analytic streaming change
  detectors (CUSUM, Page-Hinkley, EWMA, a windowed two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov
  test and an ADWIN-style adaptive window) plus a learned detector, each
  calibrated to a declared mean time to false alarm and then scored on detection
  delay, with a Monte Carlo standard error on every figure and a
  delay-versus-false-alarm trade-off curve that makes the detectors comparable at
  equal operating point. The learned detector loses to EWMA and CUSUM at equal
  ARL0 and the loss is published. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not
  certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
